      forward: "🦅 Hawkish into December 9 and nothing further, which is the whole content of the downgrade. December was never the question and is not the question now: Williams kept it explicitly, the September vote was unanimous 12-0, 16 of 19 participants expected at least one more move this year, and one post-print read has it near 88%. What failed in the last 24 hours is the attempt to extend that into October 28 and beyond, and it failed against two separate ceilings. The first is the one Williams built on Tuesday - a permanent voter and the most important voice after the Chair saying the Fed would not need to do more after one more hike - and a September core reading cannot un-say a statement about 2027. The second is new to this file and is not economic: the midterm elections are November 3, five days after the October meeting, and Goldman's published read is that the Fed will likely skip October given the proximity. That is why a core print annualising near 3.6% cannot push the October probability through 50%, and it is why the pricing disagreement is so wide - the screens are not disagreeing about the data, they are disagreeing about how much political constraint to apply. Then there is the market's own verdict, which is the part this file is acting on. The dollar is lower against six of seven majors, DXY is below its pre-release level, and the long end rallied about 10bp. A currency that cannot rally on its own hawkish surprise is not being driven by that surprise, and Wednesday showed what is driving it instead: a US credit scare is a dollar-negative risk-off, with the franc and gold taking the flow. Resolution is dated and close. Warsh speaks as a red folder tomorrow at 03:30 UTC - the only voice that outranks Williams, with no dot submitted in September, no neutral rate named and a standing objection to forward guidance, so the event is his wording on October 28 and on the path past December. PPI and retail sales at 12:30 UTC today are the corroboration check. Restored to plus 2 by Warsh declining to endorse the Williams cap and treating October 28 as live, or by a PPI and retail sales pair that confirms pass-through and demand; cut to 0 by Warsh endorsing the cap, by a retail sales miss against the plus 0.3% forecast, or by the AI-credit repricing deepening into a genuine funding event."
